(2976423, 415156, 44878, '<td valign="top">I like this picture Ian.<br/>I think it is easy to see what you were looking at from your<br/>point of view.<br/>But I would look carefully at your comments and grow from them, as they are all good comments and you may take on board what they say.<br/>I also think a tighter angle of the train coming towards the Foot Bridge would have been the best shot.<br/>Saying that, If thats what you had entered, then your critics would have been saying. I would have liked to have seen more of the Station !<br/> <br/>At least it got you out of your seat.<br/> <br/>Well Done<br/> <br/>Joe</td>', 'I like this picture Ian.I think it is easy to see what you were looking at from yourpoint of view.But I would look carefully at your comments and grow from them, as they are all good comments and you may take on board what they say.I also think a tighter angle of the train coming towards the Foot Bridge would have been the best shot.Saying that, If thats what you had entered, then your critics would have been saying. I would have liked to have seen more of the Station ! At least it got you out of your seat. Well Done Joe', '2006-10-30 18:17:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(2976442, 414027, 45475, '<td valign="top">Hmmm... well, ya learn something new everyday... Didn''t think motion blur was illegal in Advanced Editing. I love this shot and agree it''s a shame.</td>', 'Hmmm... well, ya learn something new everyday... Didn''t think motion blur was illegal in Advanced Editing. I love this shot and agree it''s a shame.', '2006-10-30 18:28:38.000000', NULL, 0),
